# Admin List Export — One Shared Visual System

All Admin **LIST** exports (PDF download and print) must use the same shared report chrome.

## Shared (do not fork per module)

Keep identical across every list export:

- page margins
- brand header (logo + company + tagline)
- Generated / Generated By block
- report-title typography
- burgundy accent rule
- filter-summary styling
- table-header styling
- body typography
- row separators
- footer (Confidential | page number | Rosewood Royale)
- page numbering (never Page 0; prefer Chromium `counter(page)` on a fixed footer)
- multi-page header repetition (`thead` repeat)
- landscape sheet fills the printable area (`width: 100%`); do **not** set sheet width to full paper mm while also using `@page` margins (Chrome scales down and the table looks narrow)

Canonical PDF template: `backend/resources/views/exports/list.blade.php`  
Shared tokens: `backend/resources/documents/contract-document.css`  
Frontend orchestration: `frontend/src/composables/admin/useListExport.js`  
Print mirror: `frontend/src/helpers/documents/documentOutput.js` + `renderListDocument.js`

## Allowed per-module variation

Only these may differ:

- report title
- active filters
- table columns
- column widths (`columns[].width`)
- field alignment (`columns[].align`)

## Do not

- create a different PDF visual design per module
- hardcode module-specific column CSS by field name in the shared template
- invent a second list PDF Blade/CSS path for one admin module
- change brand/footer/title chrome in a single list composable

## How to customize a module

```js
// ✅ GOOD — data only
{ field: 'invoice_total', header: 'Total (MMK)', type: 'currency', width: '14%', align: 'right' }

// ❌ BAD — new visual system for one module
// custom Blade, custom accent color, custom footer layout, etc.
```
